From: hmhmdcy <hmhmdcy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] chroot: skip initramfs generation for kernel=none

An external kernel has no installed kernel release. Calling mkinitfs in this
case fails before login configuration, including during install --no-image.
Honor the existing none selection rather than requiring a dummy kernel or
replacing the mkinitfs executable. Rootfs installation exercises this path.

--- a/pmb/chroot/initfs.py
+++ b/pmb/chroot/initfs.py
@@ -14,6 +14,10 @@
 
 
 def build(chroot: Chroot) -> None:
+    if get_context().config.kernel == "none":
+        logging.info(f"({chroot}) external kernel selected; no initramfs to generate")
+        return
+
     # Update mkinitfs and hooks
     pmb.chroot.apk.install(["postmarketos-mkinitfs"], chroot)
     pmb.chroot.initfs_hooks.update(chroot)
